  "body": "The dynamic kernel's MMA warps release a pipeline stage while their ldmatrix and ld.shared reads of it (generic proxy) can still be in flight, and the DMA warp then refills the stage with TMA (async proxy) with no proxy fence. The refill can land first, so FC1 reads refilled A/B/scales (whole rows wrong) or FC2 reads refilled B_down (wrong 128-column tiles). Add fence.proxy.async after each of the four producer_acquire calls (ml, fused up, non-fused up, phase2), as the dense GEMM mainloop does (#16). Fencing only some of them leaves the race: ml-only 222, up-only 249, phase2-only 251 bad of 2000; ml+phase2 and all four 0.\n\nFound by the b12x race tests (CUDA-graph replay under SM contention). NVFP4, E64 2048->768 top-8, DGX Spark (GB10):\n- before: M=64 239-263 of 2000 replays corrupted, M=256 96-99, an E64 4864->512 top-10 M=9 case about 240; never in quiet replays; worst error up to half the output max, also on the default atomic-scatter output.\n- after: 0 of 5000 for each on two Sparks; race tests' 20 MoE cases pass (W4A16, dynamic, micro).\n- unit tests: test_nvfp4_split_backend, test_dynamic_kernel_fc1_shape, test_nvfp4_swapped_token_tiles, test_mxfp8_w8a8, test_nvfp4_shared_input_scales, test_fused_moe, test_tp_moe_relu2_reference pass (test_w4a8_tp_moe and test_tp_moe_w13_layout skip without the Qwen3.5 checkpoint).\n- graph replay time: within 0.5% on the atomic output path, up to +1% with deterministic output.",
